{"repo": {"timestamp": 1784030427000}, "packages": {"com.freedomfighter.retreatplayer": {"metadata": {"added": 1784030307000, "categories": ["Multimedia"], "lastUpdated": 1784030307000, "license": "MIT", "sourceCode": "https://github.com/funkypitt/retreat-player", "authorName": "funkypitt", "name": {"en-US": "Retreat Player"}, "summary": {"en-US": "Plays retreat recordings offline, with nothing able to interrupt them"}, "description": {"en-US": "Retreat Player plays MP3s of dhamma talks, bells, and chanting during a\nmeditation retreat — built on the same principle as Retreat Timer: once\nplayback starts, nothing interrupts it.\n\n* Every recording is downloaded into the app's own storage when it is loaded,\n  so playback needs no network — airplane mode is fine.\n* Playback runs in a foreground service holding a wake lock: the system\n  cannot kill or pause it, even with the screen off for an hour-long talk.\n* The screen stays on while a recording plays — no lock, no screensaver —\n  showing the progress the whole time.\n* A recording plays only because you pressed play, and only once: when it\n  ends, nothing else starts automatically.\n\nLoading and organising:\n\n* Tap + to load recordings from the phone, from a shared WebDAV folder\n  (e.g. Infomaniak kDrive), or from a podcast feed; folder and feed URLs are\n  remembered for next time.\n* Tiles are filed into two sections — Bells & chanting on top (used every\n  day), then Dharma talks — and ordered by hand with arrows.\n* The player shows elapsed and remaining time together, with play, pause,\n  stop, 10-second jumps, and back-to-beginning.\n\nNo ads, no tracking, no accounts.\n"}, "icon": {"en-US": {"name": "/com.freedomfighter.retreatplayer/en-US/icon_uTv56QTZcPREA8HitgvFznmtrBkX3CiD_QWp8bnBjyM=.png", "sha256": "b93bf9e904d970f44403c1e2b60bc5ce79adac1917dc2883fd05a9f1b9c18f23", "size": 2941}}, "preferredSigner": "9b6ae69650b1ccf5bfa08ad15dc8b412622b8e5a3202ea066215067897a2be28"}, "versions": {"b257f242b685